A receptor function in cerebellar granule cells of ataxic mutant mouse stargazer. <source>J. Neurosci.</source> <volume>19</volume>:<fpage>6027</fpage>&#x02013;6036.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10407040</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib8"><citation citation-type="journal">Hirbec, H., J.C. Francis, S.E. Lauri, S.P. Braithwaite, F. Coussen, C. Mulle, K.K. Dev, V. Coutinho, G. Meyer, J.T. Isaac, et al. <year>2003</year>. Rapid and differential regulation of AMPA and kainate receptors at hippocampal mossy fibre synapses by PICK1 and GRIP. <source>Neuron.</source> <volume>37</volume>:<fpage>625</fpage>&#x02013;638.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12597860</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib9"><citation citation-type="journal">Hollmann, M., and S. Heinemann. <year>1994</year>. Cloned glutamate receptors. <source>Annu. Rev. Neurosci.</source> <volume>17</volume>:<fpage>31</fpage>&#x02013;108.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8210177</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><citation citation-type="journal">Jensen, V., K.M. Kaiser, T. Borchardt, G. Adelmann, A. Rozov, N. Burnashev, C. Brix, M. Frotscher, P. Andersen, O. Hvalby, et al. <year>2003</year>. A juvenile form of postsynaptic hippocampal long-term potentiation in mice deficient for the AMPA receptor subunit GluR-A. <source>J. Physiol.</source> <volume>553</volume>:<fpage>843</fpage>&#x02013;856.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14555717</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><citation citation-type="journal">Jia, Z., N. Agopyan, P. Miu, Z. Xiong, J. Henderson, R. Gerlai, F.A. Taverna, A. Velumian, J. MacDonald, P. Carlen, et al. <year>1996</year>. Enhanced LTP in mice deficient in the AMPA receptor GluR2. <source>Neuron.</source> <volume>17</volume>:<fpage>945</fpage>&#x02013;956.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8938126</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal">Lee, S.H., L. Liu, Y.T. Wang, and M. Sheng. <year>2002</year>. Clathrin adaptor AP2 and NSF interact with overlapping sites of GluR2 and play d