rotease inhibitor modulates epileptic activity and hippocampal long-term potentiation. <source>J. Neurosci.</source> <volume>17</volume>:<fpage>4688</fpage>&#x02013;4699.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9169529</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><citation citation-type="journal">Luthi, A., R. Chittajallu, F. Duprat, M.J. Palmer, T.A. Benke, F.L. Kidd, J.M. Henley, J.T. Isaac, and G.L. Collingridge. <year>1999</year>. Hippocampal LTD expression involves a pool of AMPARs regulated by the NSF-GluR2 interaction. <source>Neuron.</source> <volume>24</volume>:<fpage>389</fpage>&#x02013;399.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10571232</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="journal">Meng, Y., Y. Zhang, and Z. Jia. <year>2003</year>. Synaptic transmission and plasticity in the absence of AMPA glutamate receptor GluR2 and GluR3. <source>Neuron.</source> <volume>39</volume>:<fpage>163</fpage>&#x02013;176.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12848940</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal">Nishimune, A., J.T. Isaac, E. Molnar, J. Noel, S.R. Nash, M. Tagaya, G.L. Collingridge, S. Nakanishi, and J.M. Henley. <year>1998</year>. NSF binding to GluR2 regulates synaptic transmission. <source>Neuron.</source> <volume>21</volume>:<fpage>87</fpage>&#x02013;97.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9697854</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal">Noel, J., G.S. Ralph, L. Pickard, J. Williams, E. Molnar, J.B. Uney, G.L. Collingridge, and J.M. Henley. <year>1999</year>. Surface expression of AMPA receptors in hippocampal neurons is regulated by an NSF-dependent mechanism. <source>Neuron.</source> <volume>23</volume>:<fpage>365</fpage>&#x02013;376.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10399941</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal">Osten, P., S. Srivastava, G.J. Inman, F.S. Vilim, L. Khatri, L.M. Lee, B.A. States, S. Einheber, T.A. Milner, P.I. Hanson, and E.B. Ziff. <year>1998</year>. The AMPA receptor